Step 1: If the area of the square is 325 square meters, then the side length of the square is $\sqrt{325}=\sqrt{25 \cdot 13}=5\sqrt{13}$ meters.
Step 2: The perimeter of a square is equal to four times the length of one of its sides, so the perimeter of this square is $4(5\sqrt{13})=\boxed{20\sqrt{13}}$ meters.
